[ ] exponential : Lie A →+ |A ℂ|                                     (l.30)
      The exponential map. Currently `sorry`.
[ ] end_comp_exponential f g                                         (l.35)
      (AddMonoidHom_of_End f) (exp g) = exp ((lie_algebra_represenation A f) g).
[ ] lattice_isLattice_map : ℝ ⊗[ℤ] lattice A ≃ₗ[ℝ] Lie A             (l.47)
      (replaces the old `Nonempty` lemma lattice_isLattice, whose `.some`
      was an arbitrary isomorphism, not compatible with endomorphisms.)
      toFun is the canonical map r ⊗ l ↦ r • l (via TensorProduct.lift).
      Still `sorry`: map_add', map_smul', invFun, left_inv, right_inv
      (l.61–65). Suggestion: toFun := LinearMap.liftBaseChange ℝ
      (lattice A).subtype.toIntLinearMap (already ℝ-linear), and build
      the equiv with LinearEquiv.ofBijective, leaving only bijectivity
      as a `sorry`.
[ ] lattice_linearEquiv                                              (l.97)
      (renamed from lattice_addEquiv) lattice A ≃ₗ[ℤ] (Fin (2 * g) → ℤ)
      for g = dim A: the lattice is free of rank 2 * dim A.
